{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the congregation shall present a bull of the herd for a sin-offering, and bring it before the Tent of Meeting.</b> The sin of the first Adam and the sin of Israel in the wilderness resemble one another. Therefore the masters of truth said that the first Adam offered an ox (שור), and because of this the midrash was roused and said: why is 'unto the entrance of the Tent of Meeting' said regarding the bull, which was not said regarding the other offerings? It is like the king's beloved friend who brought a fine gift to the king. The king said: hang it at the entrance of the palace, so that all may know what a fine gift my beloved brought me." "<b>And the great</b> master, my teacher Rabbi Solomon, of blessed memory, explained that this fine gift is repentance (תשובה), for when a man has inclined after his heart and sinned in a certain matter, nothing is as fine for him as to return in repentance through that very thing after which he inclined, for then everyone will see that he admits and forsakes and has turned in complete repentance. And this is why it stated above 'and bring the bull to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting,' and it says: 'and slaughter the bull before YHWH,' and it says: 'and sprinkle of the blood seven times before YHWH' — thus far. And I have already mentioned this (Genesis 3) in connection with the verse 'and he ate.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:38.734424833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}